// `==` on an enum is not available yet, in BOTH compilers. Roadmap B43.
//
// Stage-0 refused it and stage-1 compiled it, so the same program existed for one compiler and not
// the other. No region anywhere, so this has nothing to do with the escape family — it was unmasked
// by B36's narrowing, which had been over-refusing and hiding it.
//
// The reason is in the message rather than "not supported": two variants can carry different
// payloads, so equality has to compare the TAG first and then only the payload that variant holds.
// `match` already says exactly that, which is why this is a deferral and not a gap.
enum Shade { Dark, Light }

let a: Shade = Shade.Dark;
print(a == Shade.Light);
